    "title": "Fort Smith Transit offering free rides on election day - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Edward McKinnon ,\n10 hours ago\nFORT SMITH, Ark. (KNWA/KFTA) — The River Valley's biggest city aims to make commuting to the polls easy during the Nov. 3 election.\nFort Smith Transit is hosting its next \"Free Ride Day\" on Election Day, the city announced in a Thursday news release.\nNo fare will be required for bus riders during the entire day, regardless of whether they are commuting to a polling location or somewhere else along Fort Smith Transit's routes, the release states.\nCompare the 7 candidates for Fort Smith mayor Individuals looking for route information, schedules or trip planning assistance can contact Fort Smith Transit at 479-783-6464 or visit www.fortsmithar.gov/transit .\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KNWA FOX24.",
    "summary": "(KNWA/KFTA) — The River Valley's biggest city aims to make commuting to the polls easy during the Nov. 3 election. Fort Smith Transit is hosting its next \"Free Ride Day\" on Election Day, the city announced in a Thursday news release. No fare will be required for bus riders during the entire day, regardless of whether they are commuting to a polling location or somewhere else along Fort Smith Transit's routes, the release states.",
